      "writtenOn": "2025-06-03T20:41:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this makes a copy, but maybe the copy goes away? Generally, if we\u0027re going to use `auto` like this I prefer `auto\u0026\u0026` everywhere. See https://quuxplusone.github.io/blog/2018/12/15/autorefref-always-works/ . I prefer not to use `auto` if just typing out the fully qualified name isn\u0027t too long (here I think `const SkPoint\u0026` would be nice over the `SkPoint` which is implied), since saving typing for the writer is immaterial to the amount of time wasted by the readers / maintainers over time trying to read through all the `auto`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 638,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 638,
        "endChar": 32
      },
      "revId": "ef5e1bd76f007be2f0bab26a765685237ffd6ed1",
