    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4d487e0e_abf243ca",
        "filename": "src/core/SkDrawBase.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 648,
      "author": {
        "id": 5648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-04T16:24:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are clearly lots of ways to express this (when we don\u0027t really want a mutable-ref\n\n(auto pt : points)\n(const auto\u0026 pt : points)\n(SkPoint pt : points)\n(const SkPoint pt : points)\n(auto\u0026\u0026 pt : points)\n(SkPoint\u0026\u0026 pt : points)\n\nI have landed on the first in my recent other work (when pt is a modest simple struct) -- but I bet ALL of these compile to exactly the same code for these loops.\n\nSounds like (...I think) you want me to use (auto\u0026\u0026...) ?",
      "parentUuid": "18e9d06f_5fdb7606",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 648,
        "startChar": 25,
        "endLine": 648,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "ef5e1bd76f007be2f0bab26a765685237ffd6ed1",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ee2f1920_8608f945",
        "filename": "src/core/SkDrawBase.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 648,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-06-04T16:40:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The ones that force a copy often do end up doing more work and produce longer code, even after optimization. In some cases it doesn\u0027t matter, but `const \u0026` is almost always what we want logically, since it points out that we are dealing with the thing itself (the reference) and not mutating it (the const). How that is written isn\u0027t super particular.",
      "parentUuid": "4d487e0e_abf243ca",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 648,
        "startChar": 25,
